{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e","name":"Acrobatics","source":{"id":"source:reference-0d0b7eee2953750e","title":"Acrobatics","revision":27350,"timestamp":"2025-09-04T12:03:52Z","sha256":"452cc45d073a76ff969bfb73b01f97e15e023ee8cfc8dc1aa85b86f29a564ace","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=27350","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Acrobatics&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0d0b7eee2953750e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Acrobatics skill checks are affected by an ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Armor Check Penalty"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor_Check_Penalty"}]},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["You can move at normal speed across ",{"tag":"a","children":["Difficult Terrain"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Difficult_Terrain"},", keep your balance while walking on a narrow surface, take less damage from a fall, slip free of restraints or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grappling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grappling"}," a foe, and get up from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"}," safely. In addition to the specific options listed below, you can use Acrobatics to perform typical tumbling, flipping, or gymnastic maneuvers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," You can't ",{"tag":"a","children":["Take 10"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Take_10"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Take 20"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Take_20"}," on an Acrobatics check. If you are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in Acrobatics, you gain a +5 dodge bonus to your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fighting Defensively"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fighting_Defensively"},".\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Applications"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following are the primary applications of the Acrobatics skill.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Balance"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A successful Acrobatics check allows you to move at half speed along a narrow surface such as a ledge or wire. The DC of the Acrobatics check varies with the width of the surface (see below). If the surface is slippery or unstable, increase the DC by 5. A failed check means you fall ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"}," and must make a DC 15 Acrobatics check to catch the ledge or wire. You are considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"}," while balancing, and thus you lose your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," bonus to your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," (if any).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If you are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in Acrobatics, you aren't considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"}," while Balancing. If you take damage while balancing, you must immediately make another Acrobatics check against the same DC to keep from falling.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NARROW SURFACE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ACROBATICS DC\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["8-15 cm wide\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4-7 cm wide\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Less than 4 cm wide\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Cross Difficult Terrain"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," With a successful DC 15 Acrobatics check, you can move through ",{"tag":"a","children":["Difficult Terrain"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Difficult_Terrain"}," at your normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Escape Bonds"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["With a successful Acrobatics check, you can slip free of restraints (DC varies, see below), wiggle through a tight space (DC 20), or escape from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grapple"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grapple","referenceId":"reference:4c93c2c050c768ed"}," (DC = the grappler's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grapple"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grapple","referenceId":"reference:4c93c2c050c768ed"}," check). The DC to slip free of a restraint depends on the type of restraint (see below). It takes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"}," to escape a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grapple"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grapple","referenceId":"reference:4c93c2c050c768ed"},". It takes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," to escape a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Net"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Net","referenceId":"reference:660fb2c41d028988"}," or to move 1 square through a tight space. It takes 1 minute to escape from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binder Cuffs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binder_Cuffs","referenceId":"reference:39a1390ff55032c9"},", ropes, or manacles.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If you are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in Acrobatics, you can increase the DC by 10 to reduce the time required to Escape Bonds. Escaping a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grapple"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grapple","referenceId":"reference:4c93c2c050c768ed"}," takes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},"; escaping a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Net"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Net","referenceId":"reference:660fb2c41d028988"}," or moving 1 square through a tight space requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},"; and only 5 rounds are required to escape from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binder Cuffs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binder_Cuffs","referenceId":"reference:39a1390ff55032c9"},", ropes, or manacles.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RESTRAINT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ACROBATICS DC\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Ropes\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Opponent's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," check + 10\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Net"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Net","referenceId":"reference:660fb2c41d028988"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Binder Cuffs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binder_Cuffs","referenceId":"reference:39a1390ff55032c9"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Fall Prone"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," If you are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in Acrobatics and succeed at a DC 15 check, you can drop to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"}," position as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Free Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Free_Action"}," (instead of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"). Additionally, if you are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in Acrobatics and succeed a DC 15 check, you can stand up from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Prone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Prone","referenceId":"reference:4d99dff1fb964110"}," position as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," (instead of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},").\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Reduce Falling Damage"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," With a successful DC 15 Acrobatics check, you can treat a fall as if it was 3 meters (2 squares) shorter when determining ",{"tag":"a","children":["Falling Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Falling_Damage","referenceId":"reference:4c0e132089e34987"},". For every 10 points by which you beat this DC, you can subtract an additional 3 meters from the fall for determining damage. If you make this check and take no damage from the fall, you land on your feet.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["If you are struck by a falling object, you can reduce the damage you take by half with a successful DC 15 Acrobatics check (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Falling Objects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Falling_Objects"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When falling great distances, you can attempt to use your Acrobatics skill to guide your decent. Make a DC 20 Acrobatics check to land on a target near a square you would normally land in. You can adjust your target by 1 square for every 60 meters (40 squares) fallen. Gamemasters can give favorable or unfavorable circumstance adjustments to the check based on mitigating circumstances- for example, the amount of wind or the favorable use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"},", such as baggy clothing.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Tumble"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," If you succeed a DC 15 Acrobatics check, you can Tumble through the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threatened Area"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threatened_Area"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fighting Space"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fighting_Space","referenceId":"reference:cdbf34043baceb78"}," of an enemy as part of your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"}," without provoking an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attack of Opportunity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_of_Opportunity"},". Each threatened or occupied square that you Tumble through counts as 2 squares of movement.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Additional Applications"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following applications of the Acrobatics skill are compiled from the subsequent ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reference Books"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reference_Books"}," released for ",{"tag":"i","children":["Saga Edition"]},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Catch Item"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," Whenever you successfully ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disarm"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarm","referenceId":"reference:0449aa195af99b14"}," your opponent, you can make a DC 20 Acrobatics check as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Free Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Free_Action"},". If the Acrobatics check succeeds, you snatch the object from the air. You must have at least one hand free to grab the item.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Low or High Gravity Environments"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," You can make a DC 20 Acrobatics check to negate the penalties to attack rolls in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low Gravity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low_Gravity"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["High Gravity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/High_Gravity"}," environments.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Nimble Charge"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," If you succeed on a DC 25 Acrobatics check, you can ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charge","referenceId":"reference:ff9f88ce353a2228"}," through ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low Objects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low_Objects"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Difficult Terrain"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Difficult_Terrain"},". If you fail this check, you cannot attack at the end of your movement. You can combine this with the Cross Difficult Terrain action (see above); however, the DC increases to 35.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Zero-Gravity Environments"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trained Only:"]}," You can use the Acrobatics skill to help maneuver in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zero-Gravity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zero-Gravity"}," environments. When crossing wide spaces or traversing congested areas, you can make an Acrobatics check (at no penalty) to arrive on target. As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", you can make a DC 20 Acrobatics check to lessen your attack roll and skill check penalty to -2 (instead of the normal -5).\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
